set.body:
Perform the irreversible cleanup only after every shipping consumer uses the new core.

Delete:
- MvMetric and the legacy DualityDiagram compute representation;
- MvMap/Decoder/BiProjection/CrossProjection implementations that duplicate Op;
- raw GenPca and PairedGmd compute paths;
- method-specific result records superseded by FunctionalFrame and the generic certified fit;
- compatibility adapters and stale dual-layer documentation.

Do not delete a symbol merely because focused tests are green. First prove every production consumer has a replacement and every compatibility adapter delegates to the new engine.

Acceptance:
- repository search finds no production references to the legacy symbols;
- no semantic builder drops into a parallel numeric engine;
- all parity fixtures, focused JVM/JS tests, multivar-ir conformance tests, compileAll, and testAll pass at the same committed tip;
- docs describe one operator layer and name any intentionally unsupported behavior.
